    "https://jobs.uncw.edu/postings/40709": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "University of North Carolina Wilmington Employment Opportunities | Administrative Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ's Employee Benefits Perks and Discounts Employee Leadership, Learning and Engagement Legal Notices Administrative Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. PLEASE NOTE: This posting will close at 11:59PM (Eastern time) on the posted closing date. To receive full consideration, please be sure you have fully completed the entire application before you submit for this position. This position is being recruited at the Journey level. If no applicants apply who meet the required competency and training & experience requirements, then management may consider other applicants. Salary would be determined based on competencies, equity, budget, and market considerations. Posting Details Posting Details ​Benefits of Working at UNCW At the University of North Carolina Wilmington, we are driven by a clear purpose: to empower student success, advance innovation, and strengthen the communities we serve. Guided by our strategic vision and commitment to excellence, UNCW offers a dynamic and collaborative environment where employees can make meaningful contributions while growing their careers. Located in coastal North Carolina, UNCW combines the energy of a thriving academic community with the natural beauty of nearby beaches and outdoor spaces. Here, professional opportunity is balanced with an exceptional quality of life—creating a workplace where you can thrive both personally and professionally. As a member of the Seahawk community, you’ll benefit from a culture that values well-being, lifelong learning, and connection. UNCW offers a competitive and flexible benefits package designed to support your health, financial well-being, and professional growth. From comprehensive health coverage and retirement options to generous paid leave, tuition opportunities within the UNC System, learning and development opportunities, and wellness programs, UNCW is committed to helping you thrive both at work and in your personal life. Recruitment Range $37,000 - $41,225 Recruitment Range Details The salary range advertised is the designated recruitment range for this classification. Final salary offers will be determined by the candidate’s education, relevant experience, internal equity alignment, and departmental budgetary parameters. Vacancy Number S02913 Position Title Administrative Associate Working Title Administrative Assistant Competency Level Journey Home Department Career Center - 40020 Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The mission of the UNCW Career Center is to be a comprehensive career counseling and resource center dedicated to empowering students and alumni as active participants in their own career development. Through the journey of learning, career exploration, and applied learning opportunities students are motivated to expand their knowledge of themselves and the world of work in a dynamic global community. College Career Center - 40020 College College/School Information University Information The University of North Carolina Wilmington, the state’s coastal university, is dedicated to the integration of teaching, mentoring, research and service. Widely acknowledged for its world-class faculty and staff and continuously recognized at a national level for scholarly excellence and affordability, UNCW offers a powerful academic experience that stimulates creative inquiry and critical thinking. A public institution with nearly 18,000 students, UNCW offers a full range of baccalaureate- and graduate-level programs, as well as doctoral degrees in educational leadership, marine biology, nursing practice and psychology; and many distance learning options, including clinical research, an accelerated RN-to- BSN program, an Executive M.B.A. program structured for working professionals, and the nation’s only bachelor’s degree program focused on coastal engineering. The university’s efforts to advance research and scholarly activities have earned UNCW the elevated designation of “Doctoral Universities: High Research Activity” institution (R2 University) by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. UNCW has been part of the University of North Carolina System since 1969. Location of Workplace Main UNCW Campus Brief Summary of Work for this Position The Administrative Assistant reports directly to the Office Manager and serves as the receptionist for the Career Center. This role provides administrative support to the team and plays a key part in ensuring smooth daily operations. This position is responsible for opening and closing the office, answering the main phone line, and managing the Career Center’s email inbox. The Administrative Assistant is also responsible for processing daily financial transactions, including cash, checks, and credit card deposits. Additional duties involve managing student check-ins for scheduled appointments, overseeing both virtual and in-person drop-in hours, and handling pending student account requests. This position provides front-line customer service to students, alumni, parents, employers, faculty, staff, and the general public. The Administrative Assistant also supports internal operations by taking minutes during staff meetings and updating the Career Center’s digital signage with relevant resources, upcoming events, and featured job opportunities. Additional responsibilities : Assist Office Manager with purchase orders, travel, catering, printing orders, room reservations, surplus property requests, AiM work orders, etc. Schedule appointments for UNCW students and alumni Manage Career Closet donations and inventory with support from student staff Provide Handshake support to students, alumni, campus departments, and employers (navigation, troubleshooting, account setup, event registration, posting positions) Maintain general office supplies Assist with job and internship approvals in Handshake Collaborate with the Office Manager to recruit, train, and develop front desk student workers Minimum Education and Experience Requirements High school diploma or equivalency; or demonstrated possession of the competencies necessary to perform the work. Preferred education, professional skills and experience Proficiency with Zoom and Microsoft 365 applications (Outlook, OneDrive, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, SharePoint, Teams, Forms) Experience creating professional slideshows using PowerPoint or Canva Experience developing procedures and proofreading documents for accuracy Familiarity with UNCW systems such as Banner, uShop, Chrome River, Handshake, TouchNet, Surplus Property, and AiM Required Certifications or licensure N/A FTE 1.0 FTE (40 hours per week) Months Per Year 12 Months Work Days Monday - Friday Work Hours 8:00am - 5:00pm Type of Position Permanent Anticipated Ending Date if Time-Limited Position Number 310 Job Posting Date 09/02/2026 Posting Close Date 09/21/2026 Number of Openings Single Incumbent Special Notes to Applicants PLEASE NOTE : This posting will close at 11:59PM (Eastern time) on the posted closing date. To receive full consideration, please be sure you have fully completed the entire application before you submit for this position. This position is being recruited at the Journey level. If no applicants apply who meet the required competency and training & experience requirements, then management may consider other applicants. Salary would be determined based on competencies, equity, budget, and market considerations. EEO Statement UNCW does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of his or her race, sex (such as gender, gender identity, marital status, childbirth, and pregnancy), age, color, national origin (including ethnicity), religion, disability, sexual orientation, political affiliation, veteran status, military service member status, genetic information, or relationship to other university constituents – except where sex, age, or ability represent bona fide educational or occupational qualifications or where marital status is a statutorily established eligibility criterion for State funded employee benefit programs. Eligibility for Employment Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. UNC Wilmington participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. External Link to Posting https://jobs.uncw.edu/postings/40689 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity with UNCW? (2026) UNCW Website UNCW LinkedIn Page UNCW X Account (formerly Twitter) UNCW Employee Referral UNCW Instagram Account (UNCW_jobs) UNCW Job Alert Chronical of Higher Education Glassdoor Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed North Carolina Job Network Craigslist Career Events/Job Fairs Billboards/Marquee Other * If you selected \"Other\" to the question above, please explain how you found out about this opportunity. Enter N/A if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) 601 S. College Rd | Wilmington, NC 28403 © The University of North Carolina Wilmington. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uncw.edu/postings/40447": {
      "title": "Temporary Worker/Landscaper (Multi-Positions)",
      "description": "University of North Carolina Wilmington Employment Opportunities | Temporary Worker/Landscaper (Multi-Positions) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ's Employee Benefits Perks and Discounts Employee Leadership, Learning and Engagement Legal Notices Temporary Worker/Landscaper (Multi-Positions) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note, this is a temporary position. The length of the assignment will be based on department need with the possibility of continuation. Applications must be submitted through the online application system to be considered. Posting Details Posting Details University Information The University of North Carolina Wilmington, the state’s coastal university, is dedicated to the integration of teaching, mentoring, research and service. Widely acknowledged for its world-class faculty and staff and continuously recognized at a national level for scholarly excellence and affordability, UNCW offers a powerful academic experience that stimulates creative inquiry and critical thinking. A public institution with nearly 18,000 students, UNCW offers a full range of baccalaureate- and graduate-level programs, as well as doctoral degrees in educational leadership, marine biology, nursing practice and psychology; and many distance learning options, including clinical research, an accelerated RN-to- BSN program, an Executive M.B.A. program structured for working professionals, and the nation’s only bachelor’s degree program focused on coastal engineering. The university’s efforts to advance research and scholarly activities have earned UNCW the elevated designation of “Doctoral Universities: High Research Activity” institution (R2 University) by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. UNCW has been part of the University of North Carolina System since 1969. Department Landscaping - 35211 External Link to Posting https://jobs.uncw.edu/postings/40418 Vacancy Number TSP5705PST Working Title Temporary Worker/Landscaper (Multi-Positions) Job Title Worker/Landscape Job Category Housekeeping & Landscape Services FLSA for Position Nonexempt Brief Summary of Work for this Position Workers typically assist landscaping services with planting flowers and plants as well as trimming grass and edging walks and driveways. Perform general grounds maintenance to include trash pick-up, new landscaping, irrigation installation, edging, pruning, mowing and general manicuring of all campus properties and lot maintenance. This position has been designated as mandatory personnel for the University and may be required to report to work during adverse weather conditions even though the University may be operating on an alternate schedule. This position may assist in the removal of snow, ice or debris, as required. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements High school diploma or equivalent Valid NC Driver’s License or the ability to obtain within 30 days. Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills & Experience Planning, mowing or landscape/labor experience. Required Certifications or Licensure Valid NC Driver’s License or the ability to obtain with 30 days Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit College/School Information Work Hours 6:00 am - 3:00 pm Work Days Monday - Friday Hours Per Week 40 Type of Position Anticipated Hiring Range $18 / hour Special Instructions to Applicants Please note, this is a temporary position. The length of the assignment will be based on department need with the possibility of continuation. Applications must be submitted through the online application system to be considered. Job Posting Date 08/11/2026 Job Closing Date 11/15/2026 EEO Statement UNCW does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of his or her race, sex (such as gender, gender identity, marital status, childbirth, and pregnancy), age, color, national origin (including ethnicity), religion, disability, sexual orientation, political affiliation, veteran status, military service member status, genetic information, or relationship to other university constituents – except where sex, age, or ability represent bona fide educational or occupational qualifications or where marital status is a statutorily established eligibility criterion for State funded employee benefit programs. Eligibility for Employment Number of Openings Multi-Positions Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter List of 3 Professional References Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity with UNCW? (2026) UNCW Website UNCW LinkedIn Page UNCW X Account (formerly Twitter) UNCW Employee Referral UNCW Instagram Account (UNCW_jobs) UNCW Job Alert Chronical of Higher Education Glassdoor Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed North Carolina Job Network Craigslist Career Events/Job Fairs Billboards/Marquee Other * If you selected \"Other\" to the question above, please explain how you found out about this opportunity. Enter N/A if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) 601 S. College Rd | Wilmington, NC 28403 © The University of North Carolina Wilmington. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uncw.edu/postings/40645": {
      "title": "Electric Service Supervisor",
      "description": "University of North Carolina Wilmington Employment Opportunities | Electric Service Supervisor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ's Employee Benefits Perks and Discounts Employee Leadership, Learning and Engagement Legal Notices Electric Service Supervisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. PLEASE NOTE: This posting will close at 11:59PM (Eastern time) on the posted closing date. To receive full consideration, please be sure you have fully completed the entire application, including the ‘Work History’ section before you apply for this position. Applications must be submitted through the online application system to be considered. This position is being recruited at the Advanced level. If no applicants apply who meet the required competency and training & experience requirements, then management may consider other applicants. Salary would be determined based on competencies, equity, budget, and market considerations. Posting Details Posting Details ​Benefits of Working at UNCW At the University of North Carolina Wilmington, we are driven by a clear purpose: to empower student success, advance innovation, and strengthen the communities we serve. Guided by our strategic vision and commitment to excellence, UNCW offers a dynamic and collaborative environment where employees can make meaningful contributions while growing their careers. Located in coastal North Carolina, UNCW combines the energy of a thriving academic community with the natural beauty of nearby beaches and outdoor spaces. Here, professional opportunity is balanced with an exceptional quality of life—creating a workplace where you can thrive both personally and professionally. As a member of the Seahawk community, you’ll benefit from a culture that values well-being, lifelong learning, and connection. UNCW offers a competitive and flexible benefits package designed to support your health, financial well-being, and professional growth. From comprehensive health coverage and retirement options to generous paid leave, tuition opportunities within the UNC System, learning and development opportunities, and wellness programs, UNCW is committed to helping you thrive both at work and in your personal life. Recruitment Range $70,300 - 78,159 Recruitment Range Details The salary range advertised is the designated recruitment range for this classification. Final salary offers will be determined by the candidate’s education, relevant experience, internal equity alignment, and departmental budgetary parameters. Vacancy Number S02907 Position Title Facility Maint Supervisor Working Title Electric Service Supervisor Competency Level Advanced Home Department Maintenance - 35213 Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit The Physical Plant – Maintenance Unit provides oversight of maintenance, repair and campus-wide installation of campus-wide primary electrical system and the maintenance, repair and installation of secondary distribution, equipment, lighting and electrical fixtures. College Facilities - 352 College College/School Information University Information The University of North Carolina Wilmington, the state’s coastal university, is dedicated to the integration of teaching, mentoring, research and service. Widely acknowledged for its world-class faculty and staff and continuously recognized at a national level for scholarly excellence and affordability, UNCW offers a powerful academic experience that stimulates creative inquiry and critical thinking. A public institution with nearly 18,000 students, UNCW offers a full range of baccalaureate- and graduate-level programs, as well as doctoral degrees in educational leadership, marine biology, nursing practice and psychology; and many distance learning options, including clinical research, an accelerated RN-to- BSN program, an Executive M.B.A. program structured for working professionals, and the nation’s only bachelor’s degree program focused on coastal engineering. The university’s efforts to advance research and scholarly activities have earned UNCW the elevated designation of “Doctoral Universities: High Research Activity” institution (R2 University) by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. UNCW has been part of the University of North Carolina System since 1969. Location of Workplace Main UNCW Campus Brief Summary of Work for this Position Electric Service Supervisor is responsible for coordinating and navigating responsibility for Electrical Section administration. Responsibilities include: Lead in planning, scheduling, design, leadership, supervision, training, and installation, maintenance and repair of secondary electrical distribution systems, electrical equipment, lighting, fixtures and related components. Provide temporary installation of electrical power for public and university functions throughout campus. Submit purchase requisitions to ensure availability of materials and equipment to support work. Evaluate electrical products. Standardize products and procedures. Organize, train, and lead electrical crews to install and maintain campus secondary electrical power distributions, facility electrical devices and systems, university emergency generators and other electrical powered systems. Develop new and additional technology for life safety lighting systems maintenance and compliance testing in critical science and arts spaces. Oversee interaction with the maintenance, design, repair and installation of campus systems via in-house staffing and service/installation/repair contractors. Generators Flywheel Uninterruptible Power Sources Battery Uninterruptible Power Sources Oversee contractors maintaining High voltage electrical distribution to support every critical University function directly and indirectly. Provide input to UNCW Utilities and Engineering Department, engineers, and project managers for long-term planning for high voltage resources to meet campus needs across campus. Provide condition/issues reports and recommendations to university design teams. Participate in long-term planning for aged high voltage system, requiring extensive renovations and repairs over the next 10 years. Incorporate additional and new technology requiring development of departmental resources. Leadership: Identify and communicate staffing gaps in existing resources, as well as gaps created by the extensive expansion over the previous 5 years. Model and motivate based on a Facilities-wide developed approach to issues. Prepare input and make critical decisions as conditions and business needs change. Make specific salary recommendations for new and existing positions within the Electrical Department as needed to meet the demands of critical campus electrical systems. Management: consider the business needs of Facilities, not just Electrical, and provide input on capital/human resources. Lead safety program objectives with employees, contractors, subcontractors and third parties. Lock Out/Tag Out initiative. * This position has been designated as mandatory personnel for the University and may be required to report to work during adverse weather conditions even though the University may be operating on an alternate schedule. This position may delegate and personally work with snow, ice and/or debris removal under the direction of a supervisor. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements High school diploma or equivalency and two years of experience in trade(s) areas assigned; or equivalent combination of training and experience. Preferred education, professional skills and experience Ability to supervise the maintenance of high voltage primary electrical systems via specialty contractor and service providers. Possess exceptional electrical trade knowledge and skills. Three years of progressive experience in electrical distribution and construction, general electrical maintenance, and two years of electric-related supervisory experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Strong working knowledge of National Electrical Code and NC State Building Code. Ability to properly use and train on multimeters, ampmeters, meggars, and other trade test equipment. Ability to oversee contractors installing wiring, conduit installation, underground utility repair, splicing and terminating up to 12,500 Volts. Ability to diagnose faults and perform/supervise corrective repairs on secondary distribution wiring, transformers, switchgear, main and sub-service panels, and complete building electrical distribution wiring, conduits, fixtures, and lighting. Ability to review plans, monitor work, evaluate code and standard applications, and inspect most electrical work performed on campus. General knowledge of techniques and principles involved in planning and budgeting for all electrical maintenance. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with administrative superiors and subordinate employees. Develop processes and procedures to ensure work meets applicable building/electrical codes at a minimum. Required Certifications or licensure A valid NC drivers license or be able to obtain one within 30 days of employment. FTE 1.0 FTE (40 hours per week) Months Per Year 12 Months Work Days Monday - Friday Work Hours 7:00 am - 4:00 pm, and emergency & scheduled overtime (Monday-Friday) Type of Position Permanent Anticipated Ending Date if Time-Limited Position Number 7228 Job Posting Date 08/25/2026 Posting Close Date 09/08/2026 Number of Openings Single Incumbent Special Notes to Applicants PLEASE NOTE : This posting will close at 11:59PM (Eastern time) on the posted closing date. To receive full consideration, please be sure you have fully completed the entire application, including the ‘Work History’ section before you apply for this position. Applications must be submitted through the online application system to be considered. This position is being recruited at the Advanced level. If no applicants apply who meet the required competency and training & experience requirements, then management may consider other applicants. Salary would be determined based on competencies, equity, budget, and market considerations. EEO Statement UNCW does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of his or her race, sex (such as gender, gender identity, marital status, childbirth, and pregnancy), age, color, national origin (including ethnicity), religion, disability, sexual orientation, political affiliation, veteran status, military service member status, genetic information, or relationship to other university constituents – except where sex, age, or ability represent bona fide educational or occupational qualifications or where marital status is a statutorily established eligibility criterion for State funded employee benefit programs. Eligibility for Employment Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. UNC Wilmington participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. External Link to Posting https://jobs.uncw.edu/postings/40643 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this opportunity with UNCW? (2026) UNCW Website UNCW LinkedIn Page UNCW X Account (formerly Twitter) UNCW Employee Referral UNCW Instagram Account (UNCW_jobs) UNCW Job Alert Chronical of Higher Education Glassdoor Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed North Carolina Job Network Craigslist Career Events/Job Fairs Billboards/Marquee Other If you selected \"Other\" to the question above, please explain how you found out about this opportunity. Enter N/A if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) 601 S. College Rd | Wilmington, NC 28403 © The University of North Carolina Wilmington. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uncw.edu/postings/39510": {
      "title": "​​Temporary Faculty- School of Health and Applied Human Sciences",
      "description": "University of North Carolina Wilmington Employment Opportunities | ​​Temporary Faculty- School of Health and Applied Human Sciences | Academic Year 2026-2027​ Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ's Employee Benefits Perks and Discounts Employee Leadership, Learning and Engagement Legal Notices ​​Temporary Faculty- School of Health and Applied Human Sciences | Academic Year 2026-2027​ Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Prior to the official appointment to the university, the candidate(s) selected for hire must be able to demonstrate eligibility to teach assigned courses by successfully meeting the credentialing requirements based on official transcripts and other documentation as required. Please note, this is a temporary position. The length of the assignment will be based on department need with the possibility of continuation. Employees in temporary positions are not considered permanent state employees and do not earn leave. Temporary employees are subject to the Affordable Care Act guidelines. To receive full consideration, please be sure you have fully completed the entire application before you apply for this position. For more info/to apply visit http://jobs.uncw.edu . Applications must be submitted through the online application system to be considered. Posting Details Posting Details Department School of Health & Applied Human Sciences - 31530 Vacancy Number TE135FAC Working Title ​​Temporary Faculty- School of Health and Applied Human Sciences | Academic Year 2026-2027​ Job Title Temporary Faculty Job Category Faculty/Teaching Brief Summary of Work for this Position ​​The School of Health and Applied Human Sciences, located within the College of Health and Human Services, is seeking temporary/part time faculty , for the 2026-2027 Academic Year , with the ability to teach in one or more of the following disciplines: ​Athletic Training ​Exercise Science ​Gerontology ​Healthcare Administration ​Healthful Living & Fitness Education ​Physical Therapy ​Public Health ​Tourism, Recreation and Sport ​Recreation Therapy ​Respiratory Therapy ​Physical Activity & Wellness ​ The 2026-2027 Academic Year includes the following semesters: ​Fall 2026 ​Spring 2027 ​Summer 2027 ​ Minimum Education and Experience Requirements ​​ Undergraduate course teaching : Masters degree with 18 graduate credit hours in the teaching discipline from a regionally accredited institution. Graduate course teaching : Terminal degree in the teaching discipline from a regionally accredited institution. Those with equivalent verifiable professional experience, certifications, and licensures in the discipline may also be considered. ​ Preferred Education, Knowledge, Skills & Experience Required Certifications or Licensure Primary Purpose of Organizational Unit ​​ The School of Health and Applied Human Sciences ( SHAHS ) has six undergraduate degree programs: ​Public Health ​Exercise Science ​Healthful Living and Fitness Education ​Tourism, Recreation, & Sport ​Recreation Therapy ​Respiratory Therapy (Face-to-face and fully online option) ​ ​The SHAHS also has Master of Science degrees in: ​Athletic Training ​Healthcare Administration (100% Online program) ​Gerontology with 4+1 options: ​(Bachelors / Masters) with Public Health / Gerontology ​Recreation Therapy / Gerontology ​Exercise Science / Gerontology ​ ​The SHAHS has a Doctoral degree in: ​Physical Therapy ​ ​The SHAHS also supports: ​Master of Arts in Teaching ( MAT ) through the Watson College of Education ​Master of Education concentration in Physical Education and Health through the Watson College of Education ​ ​Minors are offered in: ​ ​ Assistance Dog Training Minor ​ Gerontology Minor ​ Health and Wellness Coaching Minor ​ Tourism, Recreation, and Sport Minor ​ Whole Health and Wellness Studies Minor Yoga Studies Minor ​ ​The SHAHS is also home to the Physical Activity and Wellness program which delivers courses that fulfill University Studies requirements. The SHAHS is located in the newly constructed Veterans Hall ( https://uncw.edu/chhs/veteranshall/index.html ).​ College/School Information The College of Health and Human Services was created in July 2010 to provide UNCW with a new mechanism to link and focus its health-related research, professional continuing education, and health knowledge dissemination and application. In the formative stage of development, the CHHS is currently home to three professional schools: School of Health and Applied Human Sciences, School of Nursing, and School of Social Work. This is an outstanding opportunity to join a dynamic College that seeks to be nationally recognized for its inter-professional collaboration, community engagement and impact, and implementation science. The faculty, staff and students of the CHHS are committed to the pursuit of excellence and enhancing health and quality of life across the lifespan for individuals, families and communities in southeastern North Carolina and beyond. University Information The University of North Carolina Wilmington, the state’s coastal university, is dedicated to the integration of teaching, mentoring, research and service. Widely acknowledged for its world-class faculty and staff and continuously recognized at a national level for scholarly excellence and affordability, UNCW offers a powerful academic experience that stimulates creative inquiry and critical thinking. A public institution with nearly 18,000 students, UNCW offers a full range of baccalaureate- and graduate-level programs, as well as doctoral degrees in educational leadership, marine biology, nursing practice and psychology; and many distance learning options, including clinical research, an accelerated RN-to- BSN program, an Executive M.B.A. program structured for working professionals, and the nation’s only bachelor’s degree program focused on coastal engineering. The university’s efforts to advance research and scholarly activities have earned UNCW the elevated designation of “Doctoral Universities: High Research Activity” institution (R2 University) by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. UNCW has been part of the University of North Carolina System since 1969. Special Instructions to Applicants Prior to the official appointment to the university, the candidate(s) selected for hire must be able to demonstrate eligibility to teach assigned courses by successfully meeting the credentialing requirements based on official transcripts and other documentation as required. Please note, this is a temporary position. The length of the assignment will be based on department need with the possibility of continuation. Employees in temporary positions are not considered permanent state employees and do not earn leave. Temporary employees are subject to the Affordable Care Act guidelines. To receive full consideration, please be sure you have fully completed the entire application before you apply for this position. For more info/to apply visit http://jobs.uncw.edu . Applications must be submitted through the online application system to be considered. Job Posting Date 05/01/2026 Job Closing Date 04/29/2027 EEO Statement UNCW does not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of his or her race, sex (such as gender, gender identity, marital status, childbirth, and pregnancy), age, color, national origin (including ethnicity), religion, disability, sexual orientation, political affiliation, veteran status, military service member status, genetic information, or relationship to other university constituents – except where sex, age, or ability represent bona fide educational or occupational qualifications or where marital status is a statutorily established eligibility criterion for State funded employee benefit programs. Eligibility for Employment Final candidates are subject to criminal & sex offender background checks. Some vacancies also require credit or motor vehicle checks. UNC Wilmington participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Number of Openings Multi-Positions External Link to Posting https://jobs.uncw.edu/postings/39236 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vita Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate the primary discipline you are applying to teach for the School of Health and Applied Human Sciences: Athletic Training Exercise Science Gerontology Healthcare Administration Healthful Living & Fitness Education Physical Activity & Wellness Public Health Tourism, Recreation and Sport Recreation Therapy Respiratory Therapy Physical Therapy Please indicate any additional disciplines you are interested in and able to teach: (Open Ended Question) 601 S. College Rd | Wilmington, NC 28403 © The University of North Carolina Wilmington. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
